      "text": "Strong reactions can make independence especially important, with resistance to routine, control or an opponent's point of view. Thought may be searching but coloured by emotion, and irritation can become stubbornness or withdrawal. These tendencies vary considerably in strength. The contact does not by itself establish cruelty, and its force may be directed toward a personally chosen vocation.",
