      "text": "Strong sympathy and belief can make discrimination difficult, especially when an inspiring person or ideal promises more than it can deliver. Emotional conviction may encourage unusual religious interests or disappointment in practical affairs. The account does not require bad intentions. Its main caution concerns misplaced trust and unclear judgment when generous aspirations are insufficiently examined.",
